  "faq": [
    {
      "q": "Why can't I find the Codes button in Command An Army?",
      "a": "The button stays hidden until you complete the tutorial. Finish it, then look on the right side of the lobby screen."
    },
    {
      "q": "What should I spend my Command An Army code gems on first?",
      "a": "Troop summons are the best first pick, since better troops make a bigger difference in battles. Classes only cost 150 to 200 gems, so you can grab one later once your army is set."
    },
    {
      "q": "Why does SORRY or SHIELDBREAKER say the code is invalid?",
      "a": "Those codes were turned off in September 2026 and no longer give gems. Also check that you typed the code in all capital letters with no extra spaces."
    }
  ],
  "tips": [
    "Use the hold order when you reach a capture point, so your squad stays on the objective while you fight close by instead of chasing enemies away.",
    "Keep ranged troops like archers behind a front line of shieldmen or spearmen. Letting them sit in front usually gets them wiped out by the first charge.",
    "Save the rush order for the right moment, such as when the enemy is spread out. Rushing in one at a time against a full group rarely works.",
    "Upgrade the troops you use most instead of spreading resources across every type. A few strong units carry a match better than many weak ones."
  ],
  "useRewards": "Every active code pays out Gems, from 300 to 1,000 each, and together the nine working codes add up to 4,900 Gems. That is enough for several troop summons in a row, so redeem the whole list before you spend anything. Commander classes are a good later buy, once your army can hold its own in fights without you doing all the work.",
